        ],
        "block_content": "Team:\nAagam Bapna - abapna@purdue.edu\nCheng-En Lee - lee4649@purdue.edu\nAnthony McCrovitz - amccrov@purdue.edu\nDaniel Benes-Magana - dbenesma@purdue.edu\nJaime Xu - xu1545@purdue.edu",
        "block_id": 3,
        "block_label": "text",
        "block_order": 2
      },
      {
        "block_bbox": [
          31,
          611,
          233,
          634
        ],
        "block_content": "Sprint Overview",
        "block_id": 4,
        "block_label": "paragraph_title",
        "block_order": 3
      },
      {
        "block_bbox": [
          30,
          667,
          1182,
          746
        ],
        "block_content": "The goal of Sprint 1 is to establish Yarrow's core system architecture and implement the basic functionality needed for its primary user workflows. This includes authentication and user management, document upload and processing, search, and system administration.",
        "block_id": 5,
        "block_label": "text",
        "block_order": 4
      },
      {
        "block_bbox": [
          29,
          779,
          1165,
          887
        ],
        "block_content": "By the end of the sprint, users should be able to create an account, log in, upload one or more documents for processing, and view extracted text alongside the original document. Users should also be able to search processed document content. Administrator users should be able to manage non-administrator accounts and view system resource usage.",
        "block_id": 6,
        "block_label": "text",
        "block_order": 5
      },
      {
        "block_bbox": [
          32,
          919,
          286,
          938
        ],
        "block_content": "",
        "block_id": 7,
        "block_label": "paragraph_title",
        "block_order": 6
      },
      {
        "block_bbox": [
          32,
          977,
          489,
          998
        ],
        "block_content": "Meeting Schedule: Monday 11:00 - 11:30 AM",
        "block_id": 8,
        "block_label": "text",
        "block_order": 7
      },
      {
        "block_bbox": [
          32,
          1036,
          257,
          1057
        ],
        "block_content": "Risk and Challenges:",
        "block_id": 9,
        "block_label": "paragraph_title",
        "block_order": 8
      },
      {
        "block_bbox": [
          29,
          1088,
          1140,
          1170
        ],
        "block_content": "Yarrow has a relatively complex architecture involving a Next.js frontend, FastAPI backend services, PostgreSQL, document-processing workers, and vLLM-based inference services. A major challenge during Sprint 1 will be integrating and deploying these components while ensuring that they communicate reliably.",
        "block_id": 10,
        "block_label": "text",
        "block_order": 9
      },
      {
        "block_bbox": [
          30,
          1200,
          1188,
          1280
        ],
        "block_content": "Because this is the first implementation sprint, the team may also discover requirements that require changes to the initial architecture. To reduce this risk, the team will keep system components modular and coordinate integration work throughout the sprint.",
        "block_id": 11,
        "block_label": "text",
        "block_order": 10
      }
    ],
    "height": 1584,
    "markdown": {
      "markdown_images_count": 0,
      "markdown_images_keys": [],
      "markdown_images_sha256": {},
      "text": "Product Name: Yarrow\n\nTeam Number: 13\n\nTeam:\nAagam Bapna - abapna@purdue.edu\nCheng-En Lee - lee4649@purdue.edu\nAnthony McCrovitz - amccrov@purdue.edu\nDaniel Benes-Magana - dbenesma@purdue.edu\nJaime Xu - xu1545@purdue.edu\n\nSprint Overview\n\nThe goal of Sprint 1 is to establish Yarrow's core system architecture and implement the basic functionality needed for its primary user workflows. This includes authentication and user management, document upload and processing, search, and system administration.\n\nBy the end of the sprint, users should be able to create an account, log in, upload one or more documents for processing, and view extracted text alongside the original document. Users should also be able to search processed document content. Administrator users should be able to manage non-administrator accounts and view system resource usage.\n\nMeeting Schedule: Monday 11:00 - 11:30 AM\n\nRisk and Challenges:\n\nYarrow has a relatively complex architecture involving a Next.js frontend, FastAPI backend services, PostgreSQL, document-processing workers, and vLLM-based inference services. A major challenge during Sprint 1 will be integrating and deploying these components while ensuring that they communicate reliably.\n\nBecause this is the first implementation sprint, the team may also discover requirements that require changes to the initial architecture. To reduce this risk, the team will keep system components modular and coordinate integration work throughout the sprint."
    },
